===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of parting or dividing; [[division]]; [[separation]].
# The state of being parted.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Ezekiel|21|21|text=The '''parting''' of the way.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1949|month=November and December|author=K. Longbottom|title=By Goods Train to Gweedore|journal=Railway Magazine|page=353|text=Bridge End is the border station and the scene of many a sad '''parting''' between enterprising shoppers and their purchases—for it is a stronghold of the Customs !—and half an hour is allowed in the timetable for examination and shunting.}}
# A [[farewell]], the act of [[depart]]ing [[polite]]ly.
#* {{RQ:Byron Childe Harold|canto=III|stanza=XXIV|passage=And there were sudden '''partings''',such as press / The life from out young hearts.}}
#* {{RQ:Baum Wizard of Oz|passage=But she hugged the soft, stuffed body of the Scarecrow in her arms instead of kissing his painted face, and found she was crying herself at this sorrowful '''parting''' from her loving comrades.|23}}
# {{lb|en|British}} The dividing line formed by combing the hair in different directions.
#: {{syn|en|part<q:US>}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Hannah Jane Parkinson|title=Canvas of lies: what Dominic Cummings' dress sense tells us about Brexit|work=The Guardian|date=2019-09-13|url=https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2019/sep/13/canvas-of-lies-what-dominic-cummings-dress-sense-tells-us-about-brexit|issn=0261-3077|passage=Margaret Thatcher’s 80s power suits were scrutinised; David Cameron’s switching of his '''parting''' was national news (Cameron later nominated his barber for an MBE); and eyebrows were raised at Theresa May’s favourite and incongruous Frida Kahlo bracelet.}}
# {{lb|en|founding}} The surface of the [[sand]] of one section of a [[mould]] where it meets that of another section.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} The [[separation]] and [[determination]] of [[alloy]]s; especially, the separation, as by [[acid]]s, of [[gold]] from [[silver]] in the [[assay]] [[button]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[joint]] or [[fissure]], as in a [[coal]] [[seam]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The breaking, as of a [[cable]], by violence.
# {{lb|en|mineralogy}} [[lamellar|Lamellar]] separation in a [[crystallized]] [[mineral]], due to some other cause than [[cleavage]], as to the presence of [[twinning]] [[lamella]]e.

